    "title": "Will and Kate 'are easier' on one of their three children - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Katherine Tinsley ,\n11 hours ago James Whatling / MEGA TheMegaAgency.com _ Prince William and Kate Middleton have a soft spot for one of their three kids.\nKeep reading for the details...\nMORE: Follow Wonderwall on MSN for more top news\nJames Whatling / MEGA TheMegaAgency.com _ According to a source, Prince William and Kate Middleton \"are like other parents with young children,\" adding that \"William and Kate are easier on Louis because he's the baby of the family.\"\nMEGA TheMegaAgency.com _ \"They don't want to break his little spirit,\" the source told OK! U.K . \"William and Kate do their best to teach him how to behave, but understand these [royal] events are tiresome for a youngster.\"\nMEGA TheMegaAgency.com _ Over the years, Prince Louis' cheeky personality has captured the attention of fans. However, Kate Middleton finds subtle ways to correct his behavior while out and about.\n\"When Prince Louis misbehaved at the late Queen 's Platinum Jubilee, for example, by sticking his tongue out at his mother, Kate's reaction was praised by a team of expert commentators,\" royal expert Tom Quinn wrote in his book Gilded Youth, An Intimate History of Growing Up in the Royal Family .\nMEGA TheMegaAgency.com _ \"She apparently used a secret code to calm the children, as she does on occasions — she simply says 'let's take a break,'\" Tom Quinn continued. \"But as a former staffer explained, the children know these few words carry far more weight than we might imagine.\"\nMEGA _ After seeing fans' reactions to Prince Louis' appearance at Queen Elizabeth II 's Platinum Jubilee, Prince William and Kate Middleton acknowledged the moment.\n\"What a fantastic weekend of celebrations,\" the Waleses wrote in a statement. \"Seeing people across the nation coming together with family, friends, and loved ones has been extremely special. Thank you to everyone who turned out to show their gratitude to The Queen and her inspiring 70 years of leadership.\nMEGA _ \"From the crowds on the Mall to communities hosting street parties up and down the country, we hope you had a weekend to remember. We all had an incredible time, especially Louis,\" Prince William and Kate Middleton added.\n31",
